    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Dynamic Programming (DP) is an optimization technique that solves complex problems by breaking them into simpler subproblems and storing their solutions. The Fibonacci sequence perfectly demonstrates DP's power - naive recursion has O(2^n) time complexity due to redundant calculations, but DP reduces it to O(n) by storing results in a table. This bottom-up approach (tabulation) fills the table iteratively, ensuring each subproblem is solved only once. DP is essential for optimization problems in algorithms, AI, and operations research."
    }
